**Plan, not yet applied.**

`buildRows()` already gives full rows, `toTable()` just drops `owner`/`slow` for width. So `--json` needs no new data path.

```js
// cli.js
const jsonFlag = argv.includes('--json');
const rows = buildRows();
process.stdout.write((jsonFlag ? JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2) : toTable(rows)) + '\n');
```

`[cli.js:14](src/cli.js:14)` is the only line that changes, plus the flag check.

Say go and I'll apply it.
